course: dictionary
lesson: 3911
title: Fringe: hair, threads and edges
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Fringe is one of these words. «Owls fly almost silently thanks to soft fringed feather edges» means the soft edges of the feathers, not hair or cloth.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Cut a fringe» is about hair cut short and straight across the forehead. A scarf or rug with loose threads along its edge also has a fringe. When a sentence talks about the edge of a forest or a town, fringe means the outer edge.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. In «soft fringes that muffle the sound of flying», the meaning of soft edges makes sense, because the edges are what keep the flight quiet. If your meaning does not fit, try another one from the list.
fact: Fringe can be a noun or an adjective.
fact: A fringe is hair cut short and straight across the forehead; Americans call it bangs.
fact: A fringe is a border of loose threads on the edge of cloth, like on a scarf or rug.
fact: The fringe or fringes of a place or group is its outer edge, as in «on the fringe of» the forest.
fact: Look at the sentence around fringe to decide which meaning is correct.
exercise: «Owl wing feathers have comb-like front edges, soft fringes and a velvety surface.» Which meaning of fringe fits here? | *Soft, loose edges on the feathers | A haircut across the forehead | The middle of the wing | A cloth rug with a pattern
exercise: Mia asks the hairdresser for a fringe. What does she want? | A border of loose threads on her coat | *Hair cut short and straight across her forehead | The outer edge of the park | A new pair of shoes
exercise: «The cowboy's jacket had a fringe that swung as he rode.» What is the fringe? | The outer edge of the town | A kind of horse | A short haircut | *A border of loose threads on the edge of the jacket
test: «They built the new houses on the fringe of the forest.» What does fringe mean here? | The centre of the forest | Hair cut short | A row of loose threads | *The outer edge of the forest
test: Which meaning fits «a fringe of loose threads on the rug»? | *A border of loose threads on the edge of cloth | Hair across the forehead | A kind of bird | The outer edge of a town
exam: Read: «Owls are the night shift: soft fringed feathers make their flight silent.» What do the fringes do for the owl? | They make it sound like a rug | *They help it fly quietly | They keep the town safe from the forest | They make its hair look neat
